BBUUGGSS
       Never use ggeettss().  Because it is impossible to tell without knowing the
       data in advance how many characters ggeettss() will read, and because
       ggeettss() will continue to store characters past the end of the buffer, it
       is extremely dangerous to use.  It has been used to break computer
       security.  Use ffggeettss() instead.

       For more information, see CWE‐242 (aka "Use of Inherently Dangerous
